00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:15,340
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Madam Speaker, before we proceed with the sponsorship and plenary deliberations on House Bill No. 10858, I move to recognize the Hon. Perci Cendaña of Akbayan Partylist for a brief manifestation.

103
00:56:16,220 --> 00:56:21,920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Hon. Perci Cendaña of Akbayan Partylist is hereby recognized for his manifestation.

104
00:56:21,920 --> 00:56:34,660
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker. Magandang hapon po sa ating mga kasamahan dito sa kapulongan ito at sa mga kababayan nating nanonood ngayon, lalong-lalo na ang mga miyembro ng Civil Society Organization.

105
00:56:35,520 --> 00:56:42,720
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Madam Speaker, my dear colleagues, this representation would like to raise an important concern from our Civil Society Organization.

106
00:56:43,540 --> 00:56:51,900
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Last year po, nagkaroon tayo ng guidelines on CSO participation. Ito po ang chinampion ng ating good chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations.

107
00:56:51,920 --> 00:56:59,620
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Chair Mika Suansing. Hindi naman po ito bago. May ganito na rin pong effort noong 15 Congress in 2006.

108
00:57:00,660 --> 00:57:08,360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: It seems that while we are driving towards the right direction, this year, parang biglang nag-U-turn po tayo.

109
00:57:09,260 --> 00:57:18,580
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Our CSOs are sharing their frustration about how they are being treated in the budget process for the 2027 General Appropriations Bill.

110
00:57:18,580 --> 00:57:21,900
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa isang inquiry article,

111
00:57:21,920 --> 00:57:31,600
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: nabanggit po ng mga CSO na sila daw ay na-seen zone, ni hindi nalaman that we adopted last year's guidelines until week 2 of our budget deliberations.

112
00:57:32,440 --> 00:57:36,800
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Tapos ngayon, parang naghahabol tayo to bring them and draw them in.

113
00:57:37,520 --> 00:57:42,400
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kaya po ang tanong natin, Madam Speaker, my dear colleagues, aniyari?

114
00:57:43,220 --> 00:57:46,700
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Saan po tayo nagkaroon ng gap in terms of coordinating with our CSOs?

115
00:57:47,400 --> 00:57:51,320
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Wala na bang mas makabulang participation than their questions being read out?

116
00:57:51,920 --> 00:57:56,540
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Will CSOs be informed and involved at sa magiging amendments sa budget through the BAR-C?

117
00:57:57,080 --> 00:58:04,740
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And most importantly, nagkaroon lang po ba ng guidelines on CSO participation last year dahil nabuking ang flood control projects?

118
00:58:05,620 --> 00:58:15,260
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa totoo lamang po, Madam Speaker, napakahalagan na ang transparency in winning back the confidence of our people in the budget process in this House.

119
00:58:15,500 --> 00:58:21,600
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: What we began last year was a very significant and important step and we have to learn from that.

120
00:58:21,920 --> 00:58:26,520
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And from the unfortunate experiences of our CSO representatives this year.

121
00:58:27,300 --> 00:58:32,380
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: We hope that it's not too late for the House leadership to take this matter seriously and act on it.

122
00:58:32,960 --> 00:58:36,060
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Hindi na pwedeng ipalusot lang sa kanila na we're still learning.

123
00:58:36,600 --> 00:58:43,660
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pera ng taong bayan, sa bulsa ng mamamayang Pilipino galing, ang pinag-uusapan nating P7.2 trillion na ito.

124
00:58:43,660 --> 00:58:51,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa dulo po, hayaan po natin ang meaningful participation ng civil society organizations to define the kind of budget,

125
00:58:51,920 --> 00:58:53,500
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: that our country really needs.

126
00:58:53,500 --> 00:58:55,500
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Marami pong salamat, Madam Speaker.

