4577
05:31:22,560 --> 05:31:32,800
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Again, we started it last year to engage the civil society organizations after so many, like more than a decade of not having engaged them.

4578
05:31:33,280 --> 05:31:35,200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So please give us some time po.

4579
05:31:35,280 --> 05:31:40,120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We will look into all of these engagement models.

4580
05:31:40,500 --> 05:31:43,220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Here with us is Representative Chrisel.

4581
05:31:43,340 --> 05:31:45,620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: You know po how much I love Kong Edsel.

4582
05:31:45,620 --> 05:31:51,680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So we will look at all of these and the models that were employed during the time of Chairperson.

4583
05:31:51,860 --> 05:31:52,400
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Edsel Lagman.

4584
05:31:52,560 --> 05:31:56,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat po, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4585
05:31:56,580 --> 05:32:06,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang nais lamang po nating ipunto dito, hindi naman po natin po pwedeng laging ituro na CPBRD ang nag-head o nagsispearhead ng maganyang reformang o aktibidad.

4586
05:32:07,300 --> 05:32:15,140
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Dapat po ang mismong Committee on Appropriations ang siyang nangunguna at nagtitiyak na ang ating mga kasama sa civil society organizations

4587
05:32:15,140 --> 05:32:20,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay nagiging kabahagi o aktibong kabahagi ng pagbabalangkas ng ating pambansang budget.

4588
05:32:21,860 --> 05:32:23,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Now Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker,

4589
05:32:23,680 --> 05:32:47,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: will the Sponsor accept an amendment at the appropriate time requiring that the detailed breakdown of every lump sum appropriation including the LGSF and the FALGU be published in machine readable form under the Unified Accounts Code Structure at the time the National Expenditure Program is transmitted to Congress?

4590
05:32:51,860 --> 05:32:55,620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We will hear it at the proper time, Madam Speaker.

4591
05:32:55,960 --> 05:33:05,480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We will hear it during the proper time, during the deliberations po, as to which amendment the Honorable San Fernando wants to put forth.

4592
05:33:05,720 --> 05:33:07,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4593
05:33:07,960 --> 05:33:16,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Table 8.6 of the Budget Expenditure and Sources of Financing was released as an image rather than as data.

4594
05:33:16,440 --> 05:33:21,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Was that a deliberate choice and can the DBM be directed to reissue the entire DBM?

4595
05:33:21,860 --> 05:33:28,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: The majority of the budget, the NEP and the BESF in a machine readable format before this bill is put to a vote.

4596
05:33:28,880 --> 05:33:30,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4597
05:33:31,320 --> 05:33:39,880
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We'll take a look at it po, given that the HGAB is a reflection, is a mirror image of the National Expenditure Program.

4598
05:33:40,020 --> 05:33:44,680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So we are checking po with DBM as they are the source for that particular table.

4599
05:33:45,220 --> 05:33:47,200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Give me a few seconds po to confer with DBM.

4600
05:33:49,260 --> 05:33:51,820
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: May we clarify lang po, Madam Speaker.

4601
05:33:51,860 --> 05:33:54,400
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Which table number is it po alet?

4602
05:33:55,960 --> 05:33:59,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Table 8.6 of the BESF.

4603
05:34:02,140 --> 05:34:09,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So pwede po bang i-direct natin ang DBM to issue the entirety of the budget, the NEP and BESF in machine read?

4604
05:34:09,280 --> 05:34:13,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Actually, matagal na pong problema ito ng mga CSOs, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4605
05:34:14,200 --> 05:34:19,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hindi po machine readable yung format ng mga dokumento natin, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4606
05:34:19,740 --> 05:34:21,720
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The uploaded version po.

4607
05:34:21,860 --> 05:34:24,900
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Tine-check po, tine-test po ni Sec Kim ngayon.

4608
05:34:24,980 --> 05:34:28,140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The uploaded version is actually copyable.

4609
05:34:29,160 --> 05:34:32,260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It's not an image. It's a table po.

4610
05:34:32,600 --> 05:34:36,600
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So our partners from CSOs will just confirm that.

4611
05:34:36,680 --> 05:34:39,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat po if the good secretary has confirmed that.

4612
05:34:39,020 --> 05:34:44,960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We'll just take a look po if whether when it was translated in the soft copy of the GAB,

4613
05:34:44,960 --> 05:34:49,860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: whether the same table was lifted as is or it was converted to an image.

4614
05:34:50,780 --> 05:34:51,080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Ado po.

4615
05:34:51,860 --> 05:34:52,640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Hindi sinasadya.

4616
05:34:53,000 --> 05:34:54,920
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4617
05:34:55,760 --> 05:34:58,400
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Proceeding to my next question, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4618
05:34:58,400 --> 05:35:04,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Section 106 allows the Commission on Audit until 31st October of the following year

4619
05:35:04,560 --> 05:35:11,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: to publish annual audit reports which is after the budget hearings for the succeeding year have concluded.

4620
05:35:12,000 --> 05:35:17,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In the appropriate time, will the sponsor accept an amendment advancing that deadline

4621
05:35:17,660 --> 05:35:21,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: so that the audited record of the preceding year is available?

4622
05:35:21,860 --> 05:35:26,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: While we are still deliberating, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4623
05:35:26,380 --> 05:35:31,540
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, Madam Speaker, I would be happy to hear that at the proper time.

4624
05:35:31,640 --> 05:35:34,340
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Actually, that was something that I advocated for last year.

4625
05:35:34,460 --> 05:35:39,040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: If you would remember, during the budget deliberations of COA, it was later.

4626
05:35:39,560 --> 05:35:41,280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Dati po, December 31.

4627
05:35:42,720 --> 05:35:48,960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Pero, ado po, we negotiated po kasi with COA kung ano talaga yung kaya nila

4628
05:35:48,960 --> 05:35:50,580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: because there are also deadlines.

4629
05:35:50,580 --> 05:35:56,140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: From the agencies and then may consolidation pa po on the part of COA.

4630
05:35:56,560 --> 05:36:02,580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, at that time, last year, the best that they can commit was October 31

4631
05:36:02,580 --> 05:36:08,340
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and whichever becomes available by September 31, they would publish or transmit right away.

4632
05:36:08,500 --> 05:36:10,740
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, actually, po sinubukan ko din po yun.

4633
05:36:10,880 --> 05:36:19,480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I actually requested last year kung kaya sana by July 30 or July 1 before the NEP is transmitted to us.

4634
05:36:19,480 --> 05:36:20,460
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: But at that time,

4635
05:36:20,460 --> 05:36:23,700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: there were certain logistical limitations on the part of COA.

4636
05:36:24,040 --> 05:36:29,680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: But I'm with you on that po because I tried last year also to move up the timeline by a lot.

4637
05:36:30,340 --> 05:36:32,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4638
05:36:32,720 --> 05:36:36,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At nagkatagpo po kami ni Madam Sponsor on that particular issue.

4639
05:36:36,920 --> 05:36:39,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Last question before I wind up, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4640
05:36:40,960 --> 05:36:45,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Interpolation on the office of the President was suspended by a vote of 37-5

4641
05:36:45,860 --> 05:36:49,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: on parliamentary courtesy

4642
05:36:49,460 --> 05:36:50,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: and the question is,

4643
05:36:50,460 --> 05:36:56,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: questions on 4.55 billion in confidential and intelligence funds when unasked.

4644
05:36:57,260 --> 05:37:03,220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: On what constitutional basis can a custom of courtesy defeat the duty of this Chamber

4645
05:37:03,220 --> 05:37:09,140
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: to examine an appropriation and will those questions be answered in writing

4646
05:37:09,140 --> 05:37:15,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: or even in this plenary discussion before the bill is passed, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker?

4647
05:37:16,240 --> 05:37:19,880
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, most definitely po.

4648
05:37:19,880 --> 05:37:26,480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We will be able to assure there is a plenary deliberation for the office of the President

4649
05:37:26,480 --> 05:37:38,220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and all of our colleagues who wish to propound questions has the time to ask the budget sponsor for the office of the President.

4650
05:37:38,460 --> 05:37:46,080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So lahat po ng katanungan pwede po maitanong dito po sa deliberation ng office of the President sa plenaryo at the proper time.

4651
05:37:46,080 --> 05:37:48,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

4652
05:37:49,880 --> 05:37:53,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Last note, before I end my interpellation, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker,

4653
05:37:53,800 --> 05:38:00,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: gusto ko lang pong bigyang diin yung pinag-usapan po natin kanina tungkol sa mga reformang naumpisahan

4654
05:38:00,060 --> 05:38:06,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at inuumpisahan patungkol sa partisipasyon ng mamamayan sa pagbalangkas po ng ating budget.

4655
05:38:07,060 --> 05:38:11,720
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Speaker, Madam Sponsor, hindi po po pwede na lagi po nating sinasabi

4656
05:38:11,720 --> 05:38:16,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na transparent ang buong proseso ng pagbalangkas o paggawa ng budget

4657
05:38:16,200 --> 05:38:19,720
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at nililimitahan lang natin ito sa pamamagitan na,

4658
05:38:19,880 --> 05:38:22,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: naka-livestream yung mga proceedings.

4659
05:38:23,080 --> 05:38:26,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Transparency, accountability, and citizens' participation go hand-in-hand.

4660
05:38:27,540 --> 05:38:31,920
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At matitiyak lang po natin na tunay na may participation ang ating mamamayan

4661
05:38:31,920 --> 05:38:35,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kung sila po ay mismong kalahok kasama nating nagbabalangkas

4662
05:38:35,640 --> 05:38:41,220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: because the ultimate beneficiary, and as the Honorable Late Edsel Agman has said,

4663
05:38:41,760 --> 05:38:48,720
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: the ultimate beneficiary or casualty of whatever we are deliberating upon here in this August Chamber

4664
05:38:48,720 --> 05:38:49,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay ang

4665
05:38:49,860 --> 05:38:55,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: mga mamamayan at ang mamamayang Pilipino, mga manggagawa, at ordinaryong Pilipino.

4666
05:38:55,100 --> 05:39:01,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yun lamang po, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker, maraming salamat po sa ating sponsor sa pagsagot sa mga katanungan,

4667
05:39:01,240 --> 05:39:04,760
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: lalong-lalo na ng ating mga CSOs and POs. Maraming salamat po.

4668
05:39:05,560 --> 05:39:10,060
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much, Madam Speaker. Thank you very much to our distinguished colleague, the Honorable Elie San Fernando.

4669
05:39:10,900 --> 05:39:11,620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Majority Leader.

4670
05:39:12,580 --> 05:39:19,100
Rep. Crispin Diego D. Remulla: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Rene Luis M. Co. from Partylist Kabataan.

4671
05:39:19,860 --> 05:39:25,780
Rep. Crispin Diego D. Remulla: To interpolate on the debate on general principles and provisions.

4672
05:39:26,740 --> 05:39:33,020
Deputy Speaker Maria Rachel J. Arenas: Is there any objection? Hearing none, Representative Rene Luis Co. of Partylist Kabataan is recognized.

4673
05:39:33,020 --> 05:39:38,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker, and good afternoon to our distinguished colleague.

4674
05:39:39,260 --> 05:39:48,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'd just like to pick up on the earlier interpolations of our colleagues on LGSF and even on the BDP.

4675
05:39:48,980 --> 05:39:49,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker,

4676
05:39:49,860 --> 05:39:56,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Distinguished colleague, why do we have this funding mechanism where specific LGUs have an entitled allotment

4677
05:39:56,100 --> 05:39:59,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: then they can have a menu of items they can choose from?

4678
05:39:59,560 --> 05:40:11,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My concern is, won't this be prone to abuse depending on the priorities of the executive head of government

4679
05:40:11,480 --> 05:40:16,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that is elected and can change per electoral cycle?

4680
05:40:16,980 --> 05:40:19,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Why not just allocate these funds accordingly?

4681
05:40:19,860 --> 05:40:24,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Regarding to what is programmed in Master Plans instead?

4682
