Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: That would be under the DOF, Madam Speaker.

6812
08:33:05,260 --> 08:33:08,540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: No, the reason why I'm asking is because

6813
08:33:08,540 --> 08:33:18,680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: RA 7722 says CHED shall appoint a reputable government financial institution as portfolio manager for the HEDF.

6814
08:33:19,260 --> 08:33:20,720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yun po yung Republic Act.

6815
08:33:20,720 --> 08:33:25,180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yet the funds were transferred to Treasury pursuant to E0338.

6816
08:33:25,640 --> 08:33:29,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: An executive order cannot supersede a law passed by Congress.

6817
08:33:30,720 --> 08:33:35,340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, ang tanong po, why is the government allowing this apparent violation of the law to continue?

6818
08:33:36,440 --> 08:33:42,740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is this fiscal convenience because the national government needs the money elsewhere or wants to reduce borrowing?

6819
08:33:45,920 --> 08:33:51,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the Bureau of Treasury is an attached agency of the Department of Finance.

6820
08:33:51,400 --> 08:33:57,720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The reason why this is important, Madam Chair, distinguished sponsor,

6821
08:33:58,300 --> 08:34:02,740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: has DEPDev computed whether that is actually a better economic decision?

6822
08:34:03,460 --> 08:34:04,860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi parang ang nangyari po,

6823
08:34:04,860 --> 08:34:09,520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: iniwan natin, kaysa sa nasa CHED po yung pera,

6824
08:34:09,760 --> 08:34:14,760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: managed by a private institution, ang ginawa po,

6825
08:34:14,760 --> 08:34:19,480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: nag-issue po tayo ng executive order, tapos nilagay po natin sa Bureau of Treasury.

6826
08:34:20,140 --> 08:34:22,260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, ang nangyayari po, CHED,

6827
08:34:22,260 --> 08:34:29,600
Rep. Roberto Nazal: hindi po nababayaran ng CHED yung mga obligasyon niya sa mga state universities.

6828
08:34:31,340 --> 08:34:34,020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ngayon, meron pong economic effect yan.

6829
08:34:34,200 --> 08:34:35,360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ano yung economic effect niyan?

6830
08:34:36,280 --> 08:34:42,180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hindi po nabibigyan ng, maraming hindi na-accommodate na college scholars

6831
08:34:42,180 --> 08:34:51,840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: or students yung mga SUCs kasi yung pera ng CHED nasa Bureau of Treasury.

6832
08:34:51,840 --> 08:34:54,960
Deputy Speaker Maria Rachel J. Arenas: Honorable Nazal, please wrap up.

6833
08:34:56,120 --> 08:35:03,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, that's something lang po na I would like to, for health, for education, sana po na mamesure din po natin.

6834
08:35:04,180 --> 08:35:13,940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Let me go to my next, Madam Chair, does the DEV-DEV set a long-term objective towards a balanced budget?

6835
08:35:14,760 --> 08:35:21,820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Meron po ba tayong long-term plan na eventually, tinitignan po natin, we will achieve a balanced budget?

6836
08:35:21,840 --> 08:35:24,400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Are we gunning for that?

6837
08:35:25,120 --> 08:35:31,340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi po, pataas ng pataas ang utang natin, while at the same time, marami tayong appropriations na hindi nagagamit.

6838
08:35:32,420 --> 08:35:37,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Are we borrowing partly to support a level of appropriations that government cannot even implement?

6839
08:35:42,020 --> 08:35:48,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, well, at least on the part of DEV-DEV, in terms of a balanced budget,

6840
08:35:48,080 --> 08:35:51,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it just assesses the macroeconomic outlook.

6841
08:35:51,840 --> 08:35:54,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It gives the recommendation to the DBCC.

6842
08:35:55,120 --> 08:36:02,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But in terms of balanced budget in prioritizing critical sectors, that's something that the DEV-DEV does.

6843
08:36:03,380 --> 08:36:09,240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It also assesses our compliance to sustainable development goals.

6844
08:36:09,860 --> 08:36:18,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: That's one way in which we can prioritize critical sectors in health, in education, and all of the related sectors.

6845
08:36:19,920 --> 08:36:21,120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The reason why I'm asking,

6846
08:36:21,120 --> 08:36:22,060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: asking this,

6847
08:36:22,240 --> 08:36:25,000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kasi wala po ba tayong end goal in sight?

6848
08:36:25,060 --> 08:36:26,400
Deputy Speaker Maria Rachel J. Arenas: Your time has ended already.

6849
08:36:26,480 --> 08:36:28,120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Just, almost done, ma'am.

6850
08:36:28,960 --> 08:36:29,520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Almost done.

6851
08:36:30,120 --> 08:36:33,440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, because I understand that deficits can make sense.

6852
08:36:33,580 --> 08:36:35,400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi right now, we're deficit spending.

6853
08:36:36,120 --> 08:36:39,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: If we borrow for productive investments that generate growth,

6854
08:36:39,760 --> 08:36:43,540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: but if we borrow and the money cannot be implemented effectively,

6855
08:36:44,320 --> 08:36:47,020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: doesn't that weaken the justification for additional debt?

6856
08:36:47,040 --> 08:36:49,060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, yun po ang isa sa gusto kong tingnan.

6857
08:36:49,780 --> 08:36:50,180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Secondly,

6858
08:36:51,120 --> 08:36:55,840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: has DEV-DEV modeled what level of deficit is actually optimal for the Philippines?

6859
08:36:56,700 --> 08:37:02,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what would it take eventually to balance the budget without damaging growth and essential services?

6860
08:37:02,740 --> 08:37:04,840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, wala po ba tayong long-term plan?

6861
08:37:14,840 --> 08:37:21,100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the DEV-DEV is involved with at least the revisions and updating of the medium-term fiscal framework.

6862
08:37:21,120 --> 08:37:26,900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, these are challenges and issues that the DEV-DEV also considers.

6863
08:37:27,700 --> 08:37:28,920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, okay. Thank you.

6864
08:37:29,020 --> 08:37:34,120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, just a quick manifestation to end my interpolation.

6865
08:37:35,500 --> 08:37:37,760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Planning should not stop with setting targets.

6866
08:37:38,720 --> 08:37:43,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For me, DEV-DEV should also know what is preventing government from implementing them,

6867
08:37:44,200 --> 08:37:46,600
Rep. Roberto Nazal: what that failure costs the economy,

6868
08:37:46,820 --> 08:37:49,240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and what government needs to do to fix it.

6869
08:37:49,800 --> 08:37:50,960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Every decision,

6870
08:37:50,960 --> 08:37:51,560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: to spend,

6871
08:37:51,680 --> 08:37:52,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: has a cost.

6872
08:37:52,940 --> 08:37:54,700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But every decision not to spend

6873
08:37:54,700 --> 08:37:56,040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: or to delay spending

6874
08:37:56,040 --> 08:37:57,580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: also has a cost.

6875
08:37:58,200 --> 08:38:02,560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I hope DEV-DEV will be much more proactive in monitoring the spending

6876
08:38:02,560 --> 08:38:06,120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and implementation performance of our agencies,

6877
08:38:06,840 --> 08:38:08,520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: identifying bottlenecks early

6878
08:38:08,520 --> 08:38:11,240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and recommending to both the Executive and Congress

6879
08:38:11,240 --> 08:38:12,480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: what needs to be done

6880
08:38:12,480 --> 08:38:16,020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: before these problems translate into slower growth.

6881
